            "source_quote": "Σήμερον πεπληροφορήμην τὴν σὴν ἐπιγνῶναι ἔνστασιν, διὸ σοὶ πρώτῳ εἰπεῖν συνεχωρήσαμεν",
            "english_quote": "Today I have become fully assured that I understand your position, and that is why we allowed you to speak first.",
            "issue": "πεπληροφορήμην is pluperfect, expressing an earlier state of full assurance or settled determination, not the newly attained present assurance conveyed by “have become.” The infinitive ἐπιγνῶναι also admits a materially different reading: determination to learn or ascertain Appion’s interlocutor’s position, rather than assurance of already understanding it. The following explanation of why permission to speak first was granted strongly supports that prospective reading. The note discusses ἔνστασις but does not disclose this verbal and temporal interpretive choice. This concerns translation of the verified wording, not source corruption.",
